{"paper": "CHSL-Tier1-04-Jul-2024-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "A clock is sold for ₹550 cash or in the instalment scheme, for ₹250 cash down payment and ₹310 after one month. Find the rate of interest charged in the instalment scheme.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-instalments", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "A person spends 10% of his income on groceries, 10% on medicines, 20% on children’s education, 15% on house rent, and he saves the remaining amount. If his monthly income is ₹30,000, find his savings.", "options": [{"text": "₹15,500", "added": false}, {"text": "₹16,500", "added": false}, {"text": "₹13,500", "added": false}, {"text": "₹12,500", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "In a state election between two parties, 83% of the voters cast their votes, out of which 4% of the votes were declared invalid. Party A got 156611 votes which were 83% of the total valid votes. Find the total number of votes enrolled in that election. (Consider integer part only)", "options": [{"text": "2,58,233", "added": false}, {"text": "2,34,888", "added": false}, {"text": "2,36,807", "added": false}, {"text": "23,46,807", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "A man looks at the reflection of the top of the lamp-post on the mirror that is 6.6 m away from the foot of the lamppost. The man’s height is 1.25 m and he is standing 2 m away from the mirror. Assuming that the mirror is placed on the ground, facing the sky and the man, and that the mirror and the lamp-post are in a same line, find the height of the lamp-post (in metres).", "options": [{"text": "4.28", "added": false}, {"text": "4.45", "added": false}, {"text": "3.97", "added": false}, {"text": "4.13", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "lines-and-angles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "6.575 years", "added": false}, {"text": "8.575 years", "added": false}, {"text": "7.575 years", "added": false}, {"text": "5.575 years", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "The number nearest to 7658 and exactly divisible by 45 is:", "options": [{"text": "7645", "added": false}, {"text": "7660", "added": false}, {"text": "7650", "added": false}, {"text": "7640", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "There is a circle with a centre T and a radius of 8 cm. Two tangents KE and KI are drawn from point K, which is 17 cm from the centre. The area of the quadrilateral TEKI is:", "options": [{"text": "130 sq.cm", "added": false}, {"text": "136 sq.cm", "added": false}, {"text": "120 sq.cm", "added": false}, {"text": "127.5 sq.cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "12.5", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "In the year 2000, Monu was 3 times his sister’s age. In 2010, he was 24 years older than her. Find Monu’s age in 2010.", "options": [{"text": "46 years", "added": false}, {"text": "52 years", "added": false}, {"text": "38 years", "added": false}, {"text": "62 years", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "present-age", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "144%", "added": false}, {"text": "22%", "added": false}, {"text": "35%", "added": false}, {"text": "120%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "Which of the following numbers is divisible by 22?", "options": [{"text": "893002", "added": false}, {"text": "645372", "added": false}, {"text": "602351", "added": false}, {"text": "654320", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "Shankar covers a certain distance by a car driving at 40 km/h and he returns to the starting point riding on a scooter with a speed of 20 km/h. Find the average speed of the whole journey.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "28.8°", "added": false}, {"text": "27.2°", "added": false}, {"text": "28.6°", "added": false}, {"text": "27.6°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "Three solid cubes of metal have sides 6 cm, 8 cm and 10 cm, respectively. They are melted to form a new cube. What is the surface area of this new cube?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "conversion-and-melting", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "If 70% of the cost price of an article is equal to 40% of its selling price, what is the profit percentage?", "options": [{"text": "85%", "added": false}, {"text": "80%", "added": false}, {"text": "70%", "added": false}, {"text": "75%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "Convert 28% into the form of ratio.", "options": [{"text": "25 : 7", "added": false}, {"text": "18 : 7", "added": false}, {"text": "7 : 25", "added": false}, {"text": "7 : 18", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "A box filled with gift articles weighs 25 kg. If the weight of the box and the gift articles, respectively, are in the ratio 1 : 9, then the weight of the articles (in grams) is:", "options": [{"text": "21500", "added": false}, {"text": "22500", "added": false}, {"text": "24500", "added": false}, {"text": "23500", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "If the diameter of the base and curved surfaced area of a cylinder are 14cm and 352 cm2,respectively, then the total surface area of the cylinder is equal to:", "options": [{"text": "660 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "760 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "754 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "654 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "In the given figure, O is the centre of the circle, AE is the diameter and ∠ AOC = 100°. The value of ∠ CDE + ∠ CEA is:", "options": [{"text": "90°", "added": false}, {"text": "80°", "added": false}, {"text": "60°", "added": false}, {"text": "100°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}]}